  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="13">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:HnLond">Hn Lond</ref> 13</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" corresp="#wit-lat"><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="39" target="#HnLond_13.lnote.oe.39"/><pb n="525" ed="#liebermann"/>Et omnes debitores qui ciuibus<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="40" target="#HnLond_13.lnote.oe.40"/> debita<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="41" target="#HnLond_13.lnote.oe.41"/> debent, eis reddant<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="42" target="#HnLond_13.lnote.oe.42"/> uel in<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="43" target="#HnLond_13.lnote.oe.43"/> Londoñ. se disrationent, quod<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="44" target="#HnLond_13.lnote.oe.44"/> non debent.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="la" source="#robertson" n="13" corresp="#wit-rs"><pb n="290" ed="#robertson"/>Et omnes debitores qui civibus debita sua debent, eis reddant vel in Londoniis se disrationent quod non debent.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-rs"><pb n="291" ed="#robertson"/>And all those who owe debts to citizens shall pay them or shall clear themselves in London from the charge of being in debt to them.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">Added October 2026 from Robertson pp. 290–291 (text and translation); Liebermann’s text added from Gesetze I p. 525, October 2026 (two independent readings of the page images)</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="HnLond_13.lnote.oe.39" n="39" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">525</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">13. 14 <hi rend="italic">fehlen El</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">13. 14 omitted in El</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="HnLond_13.lnote.oe.40" n="40" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">525</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">sua <hi rend="italic">fügt zu Cc</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sua added in Cc</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="HnLond_13.lnote.oe.41" n="41" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">525</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">London. <hi rend="italic">fügt zu Horn Cust E IV</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">London. added in Horn Cust E IV</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="HnLond_13.lnote.oe.42" n="42" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">525</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">in Londonia <hi rend="italic">fügt zu Horn Cust E IV</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">in Londonia added in Horn Cust E IV</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="HnLond_13.lnote.oe.43" n="43" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">525</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">inde iidem se d. <hi rend="italic">Cus</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">inde iidem se d. Cus</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="HnLond_13.lnote.oe.44" n="44" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">525</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">q. n. d. <hi rend="italic">fehlt Cc</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">q. n. d. omitted in Cc</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="HnLond_13.lnote.oe.a" n="a" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">307</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Dass der Prozessort die betr. Stadt sei, ist Privileg auch anderswo; Ballard 143.—Nach Freibrief 1155 müssen solche Schulden und Wettversprechen in London kontrahiert und gegeben sein</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">That the place of the suit should be the town concerned is a privilege found elsewhere too; Ballard 143.—According to the charter of 1155 such debts must have been contracted, and such pledges given, in London</seg></note>
      </div>
